Company's Profile
At our client, a software company that provides solutions to SMEs, the focus is on simplifying operational processes. They are part of an international chain offering a variety of SaaS products across different sectors. Their main focus is on delivering an ERP solution to various entrepreneurs and SMEs, enabling them to concentrate on their core tasks while everything else runs smoothly. The company has offices in Canada and the Netherlands, where all their clients are located. If you have international ambitions and wish to broaden your horizons, this is a great opportunity! They have a close-knit team of about 25 employees and a pleasant working atmosphere.

Job Description
We are looking for an experienced Product Owner, or someone eager to grow into the role of a Product Owner. In this position, you will primarily focus on developing new features for the in-house ERP/CRM system of our client. Together with 2 other colleagues, you will form a strong foundation to continue developing the software. Additionally, you will collaborate extensively with your colleagues, both with the Dutch team and the IT team based in Canada.

What will your responsibilities be as a Product Owner?
Understanding customer needs and product vision: creating the product vision for the digital supply chain, defining the product strategy, and implementing the product roadmap;
Creating and prioritizing the product backlog;
Writing clear user stories and acceptance criteria;
Sprint planning and review;
Monitoring progress and making adjustments;
Promoting customer satisfaction and value creation.

Requirements
5 years of relevant experience, preferably with ERP software;
A solid understanding of the Product Owner role;
Experience with Agile/Scrum methodologies;
A passion for solving complex customer problems;
Excellent communication skills (in English) and the ability to collaborate with different people;
Creativity, critical thinking, a good sense of humor, and passion;
Preferably, proficiency in the Dutch language.

What you'll get
A good salary, depending on your experience;
28 vacation days;
Travel allowance or NS-Business Card;
Reimbursement for supplementary health insurance;
Hybrid working;
Everything you need to perform well.

Are you interested and want to know more? Great! Contact Samir Jouseiph via S.Jouseiph@haystackpeople.nl or +31645262693.
